Question 3 – Multiple GST Transactions, ITC Set-off & Challan
Your company purchases 20 Office Monitors from Maharashtra Office Systems, registered in 
Maharashtra, at 18% GST.
 Price of each Monitor – ₹24,000
 Unit Code – Pieces
 HSN Code – 8528
 GST Rate – 18%
 Invoice Number – MH/26-27/319
Your company also sells 30 Lenovo ThinkPad Laptops to BrightEdge Technologies Pvt. 
Ltd., registered in Gujarat, at 18% GST.
 Price of each Laptop – ₹90,000
 Unit Code – Pieces
 HSN Code – 8471
 GST Rate – 18%
 Invoice Number – MH/26-27/225
Create the required Purchase Order, Purchase Voucher, Sales Order and Sales Voucher 
implementing Bill Wise Reference Details.
Post purchase, 3 Monitors are found defective and are returned to the supplier. Raise a Debit 
Note and adjust the applicable GST.
Post sales, 5 Laptops are returned by the customer. Raise a Credit Note and adjust the 
applicable GST.
Calculate the Output GST, Input Tax Credit, ITC Reversal, Net GST Liability and ITC Set-
off. Determine the balance amount payable through the Electronic Cash Ledger and generate 
the GST PMT-06 Challan for the balance amount. Record the CPIN, CIN and payment 
details. Answers
1. Create Supplier: Gateway of Tally → Create → Ledger → ABC Computer Systems Pvt. Ltd. → 
Sundry Creditors → State: Karnataka → Enable Bill-wise Details. 
2. Create Stock Item: Create → Stock Item → Dell Latitude Laptop → Unit: Pieces → HSN: 8471 → 
GST: 18%. 
3. Purchase Order: Vouchers → Purchase Order → Select supplier → 75 Laptops @ ₹72,000 → 
Apply IGST 18% → Save. 
4. Purchase Voucher: Purchase (F9) → Select Purchase Order → Verify quantity, rate and IGST → 
Enter Bill-wise Reference → Save. 
5. Debit Note: Debit Note → Select supplier → Enter 5 Laptops @ ₹72,000 → Apply IGST 
adjustment → Save. 
6. GST Report: Display More Reports → Statutory Reports → GST → GST Tax Analysis → Verify ITC 
and liability. 
7. GST Challan: GST Payment/Challan → Enter balance GST payable → Verify tax heads → 
Generate Challan → Record challan details. 
